tains flexibility in the position\n\nReason: B: f1-d3 is the strongest move because it simultaneously develops a piece, challenges Black's best-placed piece (the knight on e4), and prepares to castle kingside for king safety. Development and king safety are paramount in the opening phase, and this move accomplishes both objectives while maintaining pressure.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-d3"}
