 that limit its mobility. With my Rook on d7, I'm attacking e7 and putting pressure directly on the King. This forces Black into a defensive posture and gives me excellent winning chances.\n\n**Reason:** The move R: d1-d7 creates maximum immediate threats by invading the 7th rank and directly pressuring Black's exposed King on f7. This aggressive rook lift forces Black to deal with concrete threats rather than continue their own attack with the Queen on c2. Controlling the 7th rank is a classic winning technique in the endgame.\n\n**Answer:** R: d1-d7"}
